    "content": "The Somali Federal Ministry of Interior, Federal Affairs and Reconciliation has issued an urgent peace appeal following renewed clashes between allied clans in the Dawaco area of Badhan district, Sanaag region. In a statement released Friday, the ministry expressed deep concern over the fighting and urged all parties to immediately cease hostilities without preconditions.\n\nThe conflict, which erupted earlier this week, has raised fears of escalating violence in a region already strained by historical tensions and competition over resources. The ministry specifically called for restraint and avoidance of any actions or rhetoric that could further inflame the situation.\n\nThis appeal comes as local elders and civil society groups have also been working to mediate a truce. Sanaag, a disputed area between Somaliland and Puntland, has seen periodic inter-clan clashes linked to land and water rights, often exacerbated by broader political rivalries.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, many of whom trace their roots to Sanaag, this conflict highlights the fragility of peace in their ancestral homeland. The ministry's call for dialogue underscores the need for clan elders and federal authorities to collaborate on lasting reconciliation, as diaspora remittances and engagement are often disrupted by instability.\n\nThe ministry emphasized that Islaamic principles of forgiveness and brotherhood should guide the resolution. No casualties have been independently confirmed, but reports indicate several families have been displaced.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/07/25/wasaaradda-arrimaha-gudaha-oo-baaq-nabadeed-ka-soo-saartay-colaadda-ka-taagan-dawaco-ee-gobolka-sanaag/",
