    "content": "The Independent National Electoral Commission (NIEC) has unveiled the official electoral timeline for Hirshabelle State, fulfilling its mandate under Article 10 of the NIEC Establishment Law and Article 18 of the National Elections Law. The announcement was made on July 25, 2026, in Mogadishu.\n\nAccording to the released schedule, voter registration and distribution of voting cards will commence on August 5. Two days later, on August 7, the commission will announce polling stations and voting centers. The preliminary list of registered voters is scheduled for publication on August 8.\n\nThis election marks a significant step in Somalia's ongoing state-building process. Hirshabelle is one of the federal member states, and its electoral process is closely watched as a test of the country's political stability and democratic progress. The NIEC has emphasized its commitment to a transparent and inclusive election.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development carries particular importance. Many diaspora members maintain strong ties to Hirshabelle and may be eligible to participate or influence the process through family networks. The timely release of the schedule allows for planning and engagement, whether through remittances or advocacy. It also signals the federal government's intent to uphold electoral timelines, which can inspire confidence among diaspora investors and partners.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/07/25/guddiga-doorashooyinka-oo-shaacisay-jadwalka-doorashada-hirshabeelle/",
